**Two Sum** asks you to find two distinct numbers in an array whose sum equals a target, and return their indices.

**Optimal solution:** scan once while storing each number’s index in a hash map. For each number `x`, check whether `target - x` has already been seen; if so, return the two indices. This gives **O(n)** time and **O(n)** space.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution
{
    public int[] TwoSum(int[] nums, int target)
    {
        var seen = new Dictionary<int, int>();

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.Length; i++)
        {
            int complement = target - nums[i];
            if (seen.TryGetValue(complement, out int j))
                return new int[] { j, i };

            if (!seen.ContainsKey(nums[i]))
                seen[nums[i]] = i;
        }

        return Array.Empty<int>(); // assuming exactly one solution is not guaranteed
    }
}
```

**Complexity:** Time `O(n)`, Space `O(n)`

